 {"id":"d3-fig-cars","type":"figure","src":"/images/sei/two-cars.svg","alt":"Two cars drive from Fitchburg to Worcester along the same road. Car A takes one hour, Car B takes two hours. Same displacement — same velocity?","caption":"Do Now · Two cars, one road. · Dos autos, un camino.","align":"full"},
 {"id":"d3-donow","type":"question","capture":true,"targetId":"u1.capture-pt-graph","xp":5,"question":{"prompt":"DO NOW · Two cars drive Fitchburg → Worcester. One takes 1 hour, one takes 2. Are they moving the same way?","options":[{"id":"same","icon":"🟰","text":"Yes — same start, same end, same direction","text_l1":{"es":"Sí — mismo inicio, mismo final, misma dirección"},"feedback":"Same DISPLACEMENT, yes. But “moving the same way” also asks how fast. That is where velocity comes in. · Mismo DESPLAZAMIENTO, sí. Pero «moverse igual» también pregunta qué tan rápido."},{"id":"velocity","icon":"🧭","text":"Same direction, but not the same velocity — velocity is how fast AND which way","text_l1":{"es":"Misma dirección, pero no la misma velocidad — la velocidad es qué tan rápido Y hacia dónde"},"feedback":"Yes. Same displacement over different times means different velocities. Velocity = displacement ÷ time, with direction. · Sí: mismo desplazamiento en tiempos distintos → velocidades distintas."},{"id":"dir","icon":"↔","text":"No — they must be going different directions","text_l1":{"es":"No — deben ir en direcciones diferentes"},"feedback":"Look again: both go Fitchburg → Worcester. The direction is the same; the time is not. · Los dos van de Fitchburg a Worcester. La dirección es la misma; el tiempo no."}],"correctOptionId":"velocity","explain":"Defend your answer in one sentence. · Defiende tu respuesta en una oración."},"sei":{"prompt_l1":{"es":"PARA EMPEZAR · Dos autos van de Fitchburg a Worcester. Uno tarda 1 hora, el otro 2. ¿Se mueven de la misma manera?"},"frames":[{"level":1,"text":"They have the same [displacement / velocity] but a different [displacement / velocity].","text_l1":{"es":"Tienen el mismo [desplazamiento / velocidad] pero diferente [desplazamiento / velocidad]."}},{"level":2,"text":"They have the same ___ but different ___, because velocity is ___.","text_l1":{"es":"Tienen el mismo ___ pero diferente ___, porque la velocidad es ___."}}],"talkFirst":true,"modes":["choice"]},"note":"Slide 2 · Do Now, 5 min. Quick check distance vs displacement first, then collect both intuitions before naming velocity."}
